# Released commits
- `717899e` — focus priority-only, discovery under focus, parallel default-on, fork-slot admission.
- `fc4e6e9` — `continuation.actionable` defined as the global runnable leaf count, as the user selected after the first CI attempt exposed the stale fallback-goal expectation.

Both `origin/nightly` and `origin/feature/work-parallel-20261103` point to `fc4e6e9547eecc87e9259d51d57c0616fe05c615`.

# CI and npm publication
- The first 717899e pipeline failed only in `test_work_plan_tree.WorkContinuationTreeTests.test_continuation_falls_back_to_queue_without_changing_active_or_phase`: expected actionable 2, actual 4. This was the deliberate contract decision recorded here; no production behavior was changed to restore the old count.
- After `fc4e6e9`, CI run 41744446503 completed success (quality, unit, router, channel, runtime, python-minimum).
- Publish run 41744446520 completed success at 2026-11-04T00:30:26Z.
- npm package `@one-ciel-ai/ciel-runtime@nightly` is `0.2.51-nightly.20261104-002000.fc4e6e9`.
- Registry `gitHead` is exactly `fc4e6e9547eecc87e9259d51d57c0616fe05c615`.
- Registry integrity: `sha512-X9VbMHZsDYkDTcz4DIAgnvZ1pbiRg33+25VQTWLvFS0pD7D5atQzrFGhX/U4xhL1Mp8E+sbqSEI/Aik8Xav7Ow==`.
- The `nightly` dist-tag points to that version.

# Local installation
The exact npm tarball was downloaded into `.local/release-fc4e6e9`, its SHA512 matched the registry integrity, then it was extracted and installed with `.local/install-release.ps1` using a new snapshot directory and `CIEL_RUNTIME_SKIP_PATH_REGISTRATION=1`.

- Installed snapshot: `C:\Users\djlov\.local\share\ciel-runtime-fc4e6e9547eecc87e9259d51d57c0616fe05c615`
- Registered User `CIEL_RUNTIME_HOME`: same snapshot.
- `ciel-runtimectl version`: `ciel-runtime 0.2.51-nightly.20261104-002000.fc4e6e9`
- Installed support source comparison, excluding runtime-generated `__pycache__`: 469 package files, 469 installed files, 469 matches, no mismatch.

# Installed functional smoke
The smoke ran directly against modules inside the installed snapshot, not the worktree:

- focused leaf `n8` was selected first while focused leaf `n7` waited; `actionable=5`, `held=0`.
- When both focused leaves waited, continuation fell through to another goal with `actionable=4`.
- Completing both focused leaves cleared `focus_ids` automatically.
- Discovery was enabled with focus present.
- Default parallel policy was `enabled=true`, `max_active=3`, `p1_reserved=1`, `launches_per_minute=4`.
- Two non-P1 reservations were accepted without any usage observation, the third non-P1 was refused, then a P1 used the reserved slot, for 3 active slots total.

